WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.569
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 7: Nature’s Power.

2
00:00:03.649 --> 00:00:04.499
In this unit,

3
00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:12.513
you will explore the incredible and sometimes dangerous
forces of the natural world.You will learn about natural

4
00:00:12.593 --> 00:00:14.445
disasters such as cyclones,

5
00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:16.591
earthquakes, floods, droughts,

6
00:00:16.671 --> 00:00:25.034
and volcanic eruptions.You will discover how communities in
East Africa and around the world prepare for these events,

7
00:00:25.114 --> 00:00:29.542
respond when they strike, and
rebuild afterwards.Along the way,

8
00:00:29.622 --> 00:00:35.909
you will build a strong set of vocabulary
words related to planning, science, government,

9
00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:40.846
and community action.You will also
study an important grammar topic —

10
00:00:40.926 --> 00:00:49.432
how to use the Past Simple and Past Continuous tenses together,
joined by connecting words like while, when, and until —

11
00:00:49.512 --> 00:00:53.868
to describe events that happened at the same time in the past.

12
00:00:53.948 --> 00:00:59.879
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:08.747
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use and understand
key vocabulary about natural forces, science, planning,

14
00:01:08.827 --> 00:01:10.685
government, and community.

15
00:01:10.765 --> 00:01:17.989
You will also read and discuss a text about natural
disasters and how communities respond to them.

16
00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:26.634
You will also identify the Past Simple tense (for completed
actions) and the Past Continuous tense (for actions that

17
00:01:26.714 --> 00:01:29.987
were happening when something else occurred).

18
00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.745
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

19
00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:39.551
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: conduction,
pollination, stratosphere, excavation, mechanisation,

20
00:01:39.631 --> 00:01:40.348
illustration.

21
00:01:40.428 --> 00:01:45.315
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

22
00:01:45.395 --> 00:01:49.178
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

23
00:01:49.258 --> 00:01:55.182
The reading sequence includes When Nature
Speaks and The Speech Under the Baobab, part 1.

24
00:01:55.262 --> 00:01:56.127
Read actively.

25
00:01:56.207 --> 00:02:00.782
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

26
00:02:00.862 --> 00:02:05.167
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

27
00:02:05.247 --> 00:02:09.452
The first language focus is Past Simple vs Past Continuous.

28
00:02:09.532 --> 00:02:13.228
The Past Simple describes actions that are finished.

29
00:02:13.308 --> 00:02:21.362
The Past Continuous describes actions that were happening
— still in progress — at a certain moment in the past.

30
00:02:21.442 --> 00:02:23.250
When we use them together,

31
00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:30.221
we can tell vivid stories about events that
happened at the same time or interrupted each other.

32
00:02:30.301 --> 00:02:35.523
This is especially useful when
describing natural disasters, emergencies,

33
00:02:35.603 --> 00:02:39.444
or any event where many things were happening at once.

34
00:02:39.524 --> 00:02:47.360
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

35
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:52.036
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: News Presenter Role-Play.

36
00:02:52.116 --> 00:02:56.642
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

37
00:02:56.722 --> 00:03:00.149
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

38
00:03:00.229 --> 00:03:03.793
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

39
00:03:03.873 --> 00:03:05.562
You are ready to begin.

40
00:03:05.642 --> 00:03:13.175
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

41
00:03:13.255 --> 00:03:16.866
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

42
00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:25.556
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
